  </Place>
  <Place Angle="0" AngularSize="0" Constellation="TUC" DataSetType="Sky" Dec="-72.17622418303534" Magnitude="0" Name="NGC 346 (Webb)" Opacity="100" RA="0.9849520310740464" Rotation="0" Thumbnail="https://data1.wwtassets.org/feeds/jwst/weic2301d/thumb.jpg" ZoomLevel="0.7769725615461543">
    <Description>This image features NGC 346, one of the most dynamic star-forming regions in nearby galaxies, as seen by the NASA/ESA/CSA James Webb Space Telescope. NCG 346 is located in the Small Magellanic Cloud (SMC), a dwarf galaxy close to our Milky Way.</Description>
    <ForegroundImageSet>
