  <Place Angle="0" AngularSize="0" Constellation="UMA" DataSetType="Sky" Dec="69.67928028409193" Magnitude="0" Name="M82 (NIRCam image - longer wavelengths)" Opacity="100" RA="9.931008791274728" Rotation="0" Thumbnail="https://data1.wwtassets.org/feeds/jwst/weic2410b/thumb.jpg" ZoomLevel="0.1288182218381782">
    <Description>Astronomers used the NASA/ESA/CSA James Webb Space Telescope to look toward M82’s centre, where a galactic wind is being launched as a result of rapid star formation and subsequent supernovae. Studying the galactic wind can offer insight into how the loss of gas shapes the future growth of the galaxy.</Description>
