  <Place Angle="0" AngularSize="0" Constellation="SCL" DataSetType="Sky" Dec="-36.10110581474469" Magnitude="0" Name="Webb Reveals IC 5332 (scaled)" Opacity="100" RA="23.57419156600965" Rotation="0" Thumbnail="https://data1.wwtassets.org/feeds/jwst/potm2209c/thumb.jpg" ZoomLevel="0.33665346798550616">
    <Description>This image of the spiral galaxy IC 5332, taken by the NASA/ESA/CSA James Webb Space Telescope with its MIRI instrument, has been scaled and cropped to match the NASA/ESA Hubble Space Telescope’s view of the same galaxy.</Description>
