  <Place Angle="0" AngularSize="0" Constellation="SEX" DataSetType="Sky" Dec="2.2054381351562755" Magnitude="0" Name="Gravitational lens COSJ095914+021219" Opacity="100" RA="9.987428096960235" Rotation="0" Thumbnail="https://data1.wwtassets.org/feeds/jwst/potm2509g/thumb.jpg" ZoomLevel="0.056842546431563154">
    <Description>The golden galaxy at the centre of the image is an elliptical galaxy whose immense gravity is bending the light from a more distant galaxy. The background galaxy is faintly visible as a golden arc along the top of the foreground galaxy. This gravitational lens is one of eight featured in the September 2025 Picture of the Month. [Image Description: This image shows a deep galaxy field as seen by Webb, with a distinct gravitational lens at the centre. A central golden-hued glowing galaxy in the foreground has a warped galaxy from the background as a golden arc shape on top.]</Description>
    <ForegroundImageSet>
      <ImageSet BandPass="Visible" BaseDegreesPerTile="0.008555540986259911" BaseTileLevel="0" BottomsUp="False" CenterX="149.8114239492958" CenterY="2.2054327790462844" DataSetType="Sky" ElevationModel="False" FileType=".png" Generic="False" Name="Gravitational lens COSJ095914+021219" OffsetX="8.355020494394444e-06" Projection="Tan" QuadTreeMap="" Rotation="20.039999999999917" Sparse="True" StockSet="False" TileLevels="2" Url="https://data1.wwtassets.org/feeds/jwst/potm2509g/L{1}X{2}Y{3}.png" WidthFactor="2">
